            "bug_id": 17676,
            "text": "Created attachment 2503\nImplementation of vcov.{lm,glm} as described\n\nCurrent code for vcov.lm:\n\n> vcov.lm <- function(object, complete = TRUE, ...)\n>     vcov.summary.lm(summary.lm(object, ...), complete=complete)\n\n> vcov.summary.lm  <- function(object, complete = TRUE, ...)\n>     .vcov.aliased(object$aliased, object$sigma^2 * object$cov.unscaled,\n>     complete=complete)\n\n> ##' Augment a vcov - matrix by NA rows & cols when needed:\n> .vcov.aliased <- function(aliased, vc, complete = TRUE) {\n>     ## Checking for \"NA coef\": \"same\" code as in print.summary.lm() in ./lm.R\n>     :\n>     if(complete && NROW(vc) < (P <- length(aliased)) && any(aliased)) {\n>       ## add NA rows and columns in vcov\n>       cn <- names(aliased)\n>       VC <- matrix(NA_real_, P, P, dimnames = list(cn,cn))\n>       j <- which(!aliased)\n>       VC[j,j] <- vc\n>       VC\n>     } else  # default\n>       vc\n> }\n\nThis means the need to compute everything else summary.lm() does in addition to getting the variance-covariance matrix. Further, in essence we end up doing a sqrt(x^2) round trip, leading to numeric error as compared to using x directly.\n\nSimilarly for vcov.glm (and perhaps other methods, though I'm not as familiar with those)\n\nA few years ago I wrote faster versions as a package (source here: https://github.com/MichaelChirico/vcov), but I think more properly it should be submitted here. \n\nOne remaining point is whether to remove vcov.summary.{lm,glm} methods which are no longer used internally and are unexported, however, man/vcov.Rd is using an alias for them to the ?vcov.lm page. \n\nIt also might make sense to re-use the code here in the summary methods.",
